    "overview": "3-2-5 (Teen Do Panch, also 2-3-5 or 5-3-2) is a trick-taking card game played in India, Pakistan, and Nepal. Three players use a 30-card deck. Each has a trick quota: dealer 2, player to dealer's right 5, player to dealer's left 3. The 5-trick player chooses trump and leads. Players above quota can 'pull' cards from those below in the next deal. Origin: India, Pakistan, Nepal Players: 3 Deck: 30 cards (remove 2s–6s from 52; keep 7s of hearts and spades). Rank: A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7. Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 15-30 minutes",
    "history": "South Asia (India, Pakistan, Nepal). Closely related to Sergeant Major (3-5-8 / 8-5-3) played with 52 cards. - 2020: English-language rules for 3-2-5 were published online, clearly describing quotas, trump selection, and the card-pulling mechanism. Uses 30-card pack and trick quotas; 'pulling' cards from players below quota is a distinctive feature. Popular in India, Pakistan, and Nepal; often played counter-clockwise.",
    "setup": "Players: Exactly 3. Dealer has quota 2 tricks; player to dealer's right 5 tricks (chooses trump, leads); player to dealer's left 3 tricks. Deck: 30-card pack: remove 2s through 6s from 52, plus remove two 7s (usually keep 7♥ and 7♠). Rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7 high to low. Equipment: 30-card deck. Dealing: Three batches: 5 cards, then 3, then 2 to each player (10 each). Deal and play usually counter-clockwise.",
    "rules": "Objective: Win at least your quota of tricks. Dealer 2, right of dealer 5, left of dealer 3. Player with 5-trick quota chooses trump and leads. Those above quota can pull one card per excess trick from those below quota before the next deal. Gameplay: Follow suit when possible; otherwise play any card. Highest trump wins the trick, else highest card of led suit. Trick winner leads next. After the deal, players above quota may take one card from players below quota (card pulling). Scoring: No point scoring—meeting or exceeding trick quota matters; pulling cards is the penalty/reward. - 30-card pack; three players - Quotas: dealer 2, right 5, left 3 - 5-trick player chooses trump and leads - Follow suit; highest trump or led suit wins - Above quota can pull cards from below quota for next deal Win condition: Win at least your quota of tricks. Dealer 2, right of dealer 5, left of dealer...",
