    "history": "Seven Twenty-Seven is an American non-standard poker-style vying game passed through home and dealer's-choice traditions. - Late 20th century: Circulates in dealer's-choice and home-game contexts. - 1999: Rule descriptions appear on major card-game reference sites. - Present: Still played with table-agreed rule variants on over/under handling and declarations. The core frame stayed stable, but house rules differ on whether totals above targets can win, bust, or lose tie-breaks. The game blends poker betting psychology with arithmetic hand-building and variant negotiation before the first deal.",
