    "history": "Aces Up appears in 20th-century patience collections and became widely known through digital solitaire suites. - Early 1900s: Printed in patience rule compilations under names such as Aces High. - 1990s onward: Popularized in desktop and web solitaire programs. Core rules remained stable; most variation comes from restrictions on which cards may fill empty piles. Known for simple rules and a low practical win rate, making it a classic replayable solitaire.",
