    "strategy": "Basic: Prioritize capturing the 10s of any suit; they are the fastest way to win the 'Game' point. Intermediate: The Lead: If your partner has the High trump (Ace), lead a small trump to 'pull' the opponent's trumps and expose their Jack. Advanced: Hanging the Jack: High-level play revolves around detecting who holds the Jack. If you suspect an opponent has a 'lone' Jack, lead an Ace of trumps immediately to 'Hang' it for 3 points. - Tip: Never lead the Jack unless you are 100% sure it will win. It's a 3-point liability. - Tip: The 6 of trumps is a key swing card because it can score as a turn-up bonus and still matter in trick control.",
