    "description": "Avinas, which translates to 'Ram', is the Lithuanian cousin of the German Schafkopf. Played primarily in the Jurbarkas region, it is a four-player partnership trick-taking game with a highly idiosyncratic trump hierarchy that includes the Queen of Clubs and...",
