    "description": "Baśka (pronounced 'Bash-ka') is a distinctively fast-paced, 16-card trick-taking game from the Kashubian region of northern Poland. A member of the Schafkopf family, it is played with just the highest honors from a standard deck (A, 10, Q, J). The game is...",
