    "history": "Developed in Havana, Cuba in the 1940s as a simplified, casino-banked version of Baccarat. It removed the rotating banker and player choices found in Chemin de Fer. - 1950s: Tommy Renzoni discovers the game in the Capri Casino, Havana. - 1959: Renzoni introduces the game to the Dunes Hotel in Las Vegas. - 1970s: Becomes the flagship 'high-limit' game for American casinos. - 2000s: Explodes in popularity in Macau, becoming the world's highest-grossing casino game. The transition from 'players banking each other' to 'house banking everyone' allowed the game to scale and be offered at much faster speeds. In Macau, the game is played with extreme intensity, often involving players squeezing the cards (peeking) before revealing them, even though the result is predetermined by the deal.",
