    "strategy": "Basic: Prioritize capturing the Nines. Since a single Nine is worth 9 points (more than an Ace and King combined), it is the most efficient way to build a lead. Intermediate: The 'Part Two' Advantage: Use the first 13 tricks to identify which high cards your opponent is holding. In the second half, you will know exactly which suits they are void in. Advanced: Trump Control: Save your 'Don' (5 of trumps) to capture an opponent's high-point Nine when they are forced to lead it or play it on a side-suit void. - Tip: Never lead a Nine unless you are certain it will win the trick. - Tip: Count the trumps carefully; there are 13 in total across both phases.",
