    "strategy": "Basic: In 1-card rounds, an Ace is a guaranteed trick. In higher rounds, bid conservatively—it is usually easier to win an extra trick than to lose one you didn't want. Intermediate: Counting the Total: Pay attention to the sum of the bids. If the total is much higher than the tricks available, play defensively as players will be fighting over every trick. Advanced: The Dealer's Trap: As the dealer, use your forced-bid constraint to create a 'low-bid' round if you have a weak hand, forcing others to fight for high tricks while you safely duck with your low cards. - Tip: Bidding zero is often the hardest and most rewarding strategy. - Tip: Track the high trumps—knowing if the King of trumps is still out determines if your Queen is a safe winner.",
