    "history": "Boomke Wies is a Belgian card game from the Whist family, played in fixed partnerships with an auction mechanic. It is distinct from classic Whist through its bidding system, though a simpler non-bidding variant exists that closely mirrors traditional Whist. - Traditional: Evolved from the Whist family in Belgium. - Present: Actively played in Belgian clubs and tournaments. The International World Whist Association organises tournaments. The game exists in two forms: the auction version (described here) and a simpler version without bidding that essentially IS classic Whist with turned-up trump. The auction version adds significant strategic depth. Part of the rich Belgian card game tradition alongside Wiezen, Kleurenwiezen, and other Whist variants. Tournament play is organised by the International World Whist Association (IWWA).",
