    "history": "4-Card Brag developed as a popular regional variant in the UK, designed to provide more player agency than the strictly deterministic deal of 3-Card Brag. It is particularly common in casual pub games where players want slightly 'bigger' hands to play with. - Mid-20th Century: Multi-card Brag variants gain popularity in British card clubs. - 1980s: Standardized as a common Dealer's Choice option. - Present: A frequent favorite in online Brag communities. The game retains all the core 'Blind' and 'See' rules of its parent but adds a 'Pre-Vying' phase where hands are optimized. Reflects the British preference for card games that allow for skill-based selection and tactical 'mucking'.",
