    "overview": "Seven Card Brag is a partition variant related to Crash and Six Card Brag. Each player receives seven cards, normally discards one, and divides the remaining six into two three-card Brag hands for comparison. Origin: Great Britain Players: 2-6 Deck: 52-card standard deck Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 20-40 minutes",
    "history": "Developed as a high-skill extension of standard 3-Card Brag, 7-Card Brag appeared in card rooms as a faster-playing alternative to 9-Card Brag (Crash). It emphasizes the tactical discard of the seventh card to perfectly balance two hands. - Mid-20th Century: Multi-hand Brag variants evolve in the UK. - 1980s: 7-Card variant becomes a staple of high-stakes social gaming. - Present: Popular in British card clubs and as a digital competitive format. The addition of a seventh card and a muck mechanic allows for much more flexible hand construction than the rigid 6-card or 9-card partition variants. Regarded as a game of 'perfect balance', where the ability to split 7 cards into two winning three-card units is the hallmark of a master player.",
