    "rules": "Objective: Win the pot by having the highest-ranked hands across the partition or by forcing others to fold. Gameplay: 1. **Partition**: Players split 7 cards into Hand A (3 cards), Hand B (3 cards), and 1 Muck card. 2. **Vying**: Standard Brag betting follows. Players choose to play 'Blind' (before seeing the 7 cards) or 'See'. 3. **Ranks**: Prial > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card. Scoring: Standard pot-based resolution across dual-hand comparisons. - Both three-card hands must be legal Brag combinations. - In many house rules, a player must win both comparisons to sweep the pot. - A Seeing player bets double the cost of a Blind player. Win condition: Win both hand comparisons OR be the last player standing.",
    "strategy": "Basic: Use the seventh card to remove a rank that doesn't fit into a pair or sequence. With 7 cards, you should aim for at least two Flushes or one strong Run. Intermediate: The 'Sacrifice' Discard: If you have a choice between making one almost-unbeatable Prial or two very strong Runs, the two Runs are often statistically safer for winning multi-hand comparisons. Advanced: Kicker Optimization: When building your two hands, ensure Hand B (the weaker hand) has the highest possible kickers. Many rounds are won on Hand B tie-breakers. - Tip: Track the mucked cards in your head—knowing which ranks are 'dead' helps you read opponent partitions. - Tip: Don't ignore the Blind bet; the half-price advantage is massive even with 7 cards to choose from.",
