    "rules": "Objective: Win enough tricks to fulfill the contract, using both your hand and your designated dummy hand. Gameplay: 1. **Auction**: Players bid for trumps as in standard Bridge. 2. **Play**: Each turn involves playing two cards—one from the player's hand and one from their dummy. 3. **Uncovering**: When a face-up dummy card is played, the face-down card beneath it is flipped over and becomes available for the next trick. Scoring: Standard Bridge scoring with two-player adjustments. - Must follow suit from the specific source hand (Player Hand or Dummy Hand). - The highest card among the four cards played wins the trick for the team. - Standard Bridge bidding and scoring applies. Win condition: Fulfill the contract or reach target match score.",
