    "setup": "Players: Minimum Players: 3 Maximum Players: 6 Optimal Players: 4-5 Partnerships: No, each plays for themselves Deck: Type: Standard 52-card pack Number of Decks: 1 Jokers: Optional (can be wild) Alternative: Multiple decks for large groups Equipment: Standard 52-card pack Table space for discard pile Dealing: Cards per Player: All cards dealt evenly Dealing Pattern: Clockwise Card visibility: Players keep cards face down, count visible to others",
    "rules": "Objective: Be the first player to get rid of all your cards by playing them to a central pile, either honestly or by bluffing about their rank. Gameplay: The game begins with aces (or a chosen rank). The first player plays one or more cards face down, claiming they are aces. Play proceeds clockwise with next rank (2s, then 3s, etc.). After kings, it cycles back to aces. Players can play honestly or bluff. After any play, any other player can challenge by calling 'Bullshit!', 'Cheat!', or 'I Doubt It!'. The played cards are revealed. If the player was lying, they take the entire discard pile. If telling truth, the challenger takes the pile. The winner is first to empty their hand. Scoring: First player to get rid of all their cards and survive any challenge resulting from their final play wins the deal. Tables that track scores across multiple deals can award one penalty point per card...",
