    "setup": "Players: Minimum Players: 2 Maximum Players: 8 Optimal Players: 4-5 Partnerships: No, each plays for themselves Deck: Type: 48-card Spanish-suited pack Number of Decks: 1 Card Ranks: King (high), Horse, Maid, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1/Ace (low) Alternative: 40-card pack (omit 9s and 8s) Equipment: 48-card Spanish pack (or 40-card) Score sheet for penalty points Table space Dealing: Cards per Player: 4 cards each Dealing Pattern: Anticlockwise, one card at a time Stock: Remaining cards form face-down drawing stock",
    "rules": "Objective: Be the first player to play all your cards. The last player holding cards loses the hand and receives a penalty point. Gameplay: The player to dealer's right leads any card. Other players must follow suit. A player who cannot follow suit must draw cards one at a time from the stock until finding a card of the required suit, which must then be played. The highest card of the led suit wins the trick, and the winner leads to the next trick. If the stock runs out, players who cannot follow suit simply pass without playing. Scoring: Each hand, the last player left holding cards receives a penalty point. The game is played over multiple hands until someone accumulates the agreed number of penalty points and loses. - Must follow suit if possible - If unable to follow, draw from stock until finding playable card - Highest card of led suit wins the trick - Winner of trick leads to...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Try to maintain cards in multiple suits to avoid being forced to draw. Play high cards early to win tricks and control the lead. When you have the lead, choose suits where you have strength. Intermediate: Pay attention to which suits opponents are struggling with. If you notice a player passing on a suit, they may be accumulating cards - consider leading that suit to force them to draw more. Advanced: Card counting is valuable - track which high cards have been played. If you know the King and Horse of a suit have been played, your Maid becomes the highest card. Balance winning tricks (to control the lead) against playing cards quickly. - Tip: Don't hold onto high cards too long - you need to win tricks to control play - Tip: Watch opponents' drawing patterns to deduce their hand composition - Tip: If stock is low, be cautious about playing your last card of a suit - Tip: When...",
