    "history": "Calypso was invented in Trinidad around the 1940s. It gained international attention in the 1950s following promotion by bridge authority Ely Culbertson who championed it as a potential rival to Contract Bridge. - 1940s: Invented in Trinidad. - 1950s: Promoted internationally, particularly in the UK and USA. - 1960s-present: A cult favourite among trick-taking enthusiasts. The personal-trump concept is unique among widely played trick-taking games. Using four 52-card decks gives each player multiple copies of cards in their trump suit. Named after the Trinidadian musical tradition. The game reflects Caribbean creativity in card game design.",
