    "strategy": "Basic: Race to your first canastaâ€”you cannot go out without one. Hoard wild cards; don't waste them on early small melds. Intermediate: Discard Pile Control: Never discard a card that gives your opponent an easy pile takeback. Coordinate with partner on which ranks to pursueâ€”don't overlap efforts. Advanced: Freeze the Pile: Discard a wild card (freezing) when opponents are about to take a large pile. Timing of going out is crucialâ€”go out when you maximize your card-point lead and prevent opponent's canastas. - Tip: Red threes are pure bonus pointsâ€”lay them immediately and draw. - Tip: In the late game, use wild cards to complete your canasta quickly and go out.",
