    "history": "Indonesia. Cangkul ('to dig with a hoe'): shedding game; 3â€“5p, 52 cards, 7 each. Follow suit; can't follow = draw from stock until playable; stock empty = pass and pick up trick. Similar to Burro in Spain and Donkey in Goa. - Traditional origins: Played for generations in Indonesia - Modern Era: Remains one of the most popular Indonesian card games - Related games: Spanish Burro and Goan Donkey share similar mechanics - Rules codified in written form and shared in English with input from regional players The core game has remained stable. Some variants add jokers as wild cards that win tricks. The name reflects Indonesian agricultural heritage - the cangkul is a traditional farming tool. The game is played casually in homes and coffee shops.",
