    "rules": "Objective: Be the first player to play all your cards. Winner is first to empty their hand. Gameplay: The player to dealer's left leads any card. Other players must follow suit if possible. The highest card of the led suit wins the trick, and the winner leads to the next trick. If a player cannot follow suit, they must draw cards from the stock one at a time until finding a card of the required suit, which must be played immediately. If the stock is empty and a player cannot follow, they don't play to that trick and must pick up all cards from the incomplete trick at the end, adding them to their hand. Scoring: First player to empty their hand wins the round; no card point values. - 7 cards dealt to each player - Must follow suit if possible - Highest card of led suit wins trick - Winner of trick leads to next trick - If cannot follow suit, draw from stock until finding playable card -...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Try to maintain cards in multiple suits. Play high cards to win tricks when you have strength in a suit. When leading with the stock low, consider leading suits where opponents may be forced to pass. Intermediate: Pay attention to which suits opponents are drawing for. If you win a trick and the stock is low, leading a suit where you saw someone drawing can force them to pass and take cards. Advanced: Card counting to track which high cards remain. Strategic use of the joker if playing with one. Managing hand size - sometimes it's better to pass and take cards if you can then control play. - Tip: Keep variety in your hand - don't play all cards of one suit - Tip: Winning tricks lets you control the lead - Tip: Watch for opponents who have to draw frequently - Tip: When stock is low, be careful about playing your last card of a suit - Tip: If you have the joker, save it for when...",
