    "history": "Caribbean Stud Poker is believed to have been developed in the 1980s, allegedly by poker professional David Sklansky (originally as 'Casino Poker'). It spread through Caribbean cruise ships and casinos, reaching land-based casinos in the late 1980s and 1990s. - Mid-1980s: Game developed; patented. - Late 1980s: Introduced in Caribbean casinos and cruise ships. - 1990s: Spread to US, European, and global casinos. - 2000s-present: Progressive jackpot side bet becomes a standard feature. Its 'dealer must qualify' mechanic differentiates it from straight poker. The progressive jackpot, usually seeded at $10,000, creates huge prize appeal. One of the most widely played casino poker variants globally.",
