    "rules": "Objective: Be the first player to discard all cards from your hand. Gameplay: 1. Starting Play: The player to the dealer's left goes first, then play proceeds clockwise 2. Taking Turns: On your turn, you must either play a valid card or draw from the stock pile 3. Playing Cards: Match the top card of the discard pile by rank, suit, or play a wild 8 4. Drawing: If you cannot play, draw cards from the stock pile until you can play (or draw one card depending on house rules) 5. Winning: The first player to play their last card wins the round Scoring: Be the first player to discard all cards from your hand. - Matching: A card must match the top discard card by rank OR suit (unless it's an 8) - Wild 8s: 8s can be played on any card regardless of rank or suit - Declaring Suit: When playing an 8, the player immediately declares the new suit to be matched - Stock Pile: If the stock pile runs...",
    "strategy": "Basic: For Beginners 1. Save Your 8s: Keep 8s for emergencies when you cannot match the discard pile 2. Change Suits Wisely: When playing an 8, choose a suit you have multiple cards of 3. Force Draws: Play 2s strategically to make opponents draw cards 4. Pay Attention: Watch what cards other players are picking up to deduce their hands 5. Suit Management: Try to reduce the number of different suits in your hand Intermediate: Card Counting: Keep track of which 8s have been played Suit Control: Change suits to ones you know opponents don't have Timing Reverses: Use Aces to give yourself multiple turns in 2-player games Skip Chains: Coordinate Queens to skip dangerous opponents Advanced: Bluffing with 8s: Play an 8 early to mislead opponents about your hand composition Draw Pile Management: Control when opponents are forced to draw Endgame Planning: Plan your final cards to ensure you can...",
