    "history": "Cucumber appears in Nordic student card culture and is documented with national variants such as Agurk and Gurka. - Mid-20th century: Early documented forms in Scandinavian card books. - 1970s-1980s: Popular student game across Denmark, Sweden, Finland and neighbors. Regional variants alter the beat rule and scoring thresholds while keeping the lose-last-trick core. Known for reverse-pressure trick play where high cards can become liabilities late.",
