    "history": "Cuttle's exact origins are unclear but it is believed to be an extremely old English card game, possibly dating to the 17th century. It gained a modern following through the online platform cuttle.cards which created a standardised ruleset and competitive scene. - Possibly 17th century: Origins in England. - 20th century: Documented in American card game books. - 2010s-present: Revival via online competitive play at cuttle.cards. The modern standardised ruleset clarified card abilities and made the game competitive. A growing online community now runs tournaments. One of the few ancient card games with a thriving modern competitive digital community.",
