    "history": "Donkey is a localized variant of the international family of 'Get Away' or 'Spoons' games. It has been a staple in Indian households for generations, specifically across Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Andhra Pradesh, and Karnataka. - 20th Century: Becomes a standard family game across the Indian subcontinent. - Modern Era: Often played by children and students during festivities or social gatherings. The game evolved to emphasize the 'shame' of being the last player (the Donkey), often involving lighthearted penalties or nicknames for the loser. In South India, the game is highndenergy and vocal, with players shouting 'Kazhuda!' (Donkey) as soon as someone is forced to pick up cards.",
