    "strategy": "Basic: If your partner has won a trick and it is sitting in the center, play your best cards to help them win the very next trick for a doublendwin. Intermediate: Trump Control: Use your small trumps to 'break' the opponent's consecutive win. If an opponent wins a trick, use a trump on the next trick even if it's unlikely to win the whole round, just to prevent them from getting two in a row. Advanced: Baiting: Intentionally play a mediocre card after your team has won a trick to bait the opponent into overplaying, then counter with a high trump to secure the consecutive win. - Tip: The first 5 cards are the most important for choosing the trump suit. Choose a suit where you have high honors (Ace/King). - Tip: Pay attention to the center pileâ€”the bigger the pile, the more aggressive you should be with your high cards.",
