    "setup": "Players: Best with 4 players. Deck: 32ndcard Germanndsuited pack: Acorns (žaludy), Leaves (zelené), Hearts (červené), Balls (kule). Equipment: German-suited deck (A, K, O, U, 10, 9, 8, 7). Dealing: Usually 4nd6 cards to each player (common variation handles all 32 cards being dealt).",
    "rules": "Objective: Be the first to shed all cards. Avoid being the last player left with cards. Gameplay: 1. Attacking: One player leads a card (the attack). 2. Defending: The defender must play a higher card of the same suit or a trump. 3. Beating cards: If a defender beats all attacking cards, the cards are discarded (Vejbit). 4. Failure: If a defender cannot beat a card, they must pick up common pile. Scoring: Scoring uses the documented rules for Dudák and determines round or match winners accordingly. - Hearts are often the permanent trump suit. - Attacking cards must match the rank of any card currently on the table to continue an attack. - In 'Secret Dudák,' trumps are revealed midndhand by the first player who chooses to do so. Win condition: Be the first to shed all cards. Avoid being the last player left with cards.",
    "strategy": "Basic: Save your trumps for late in the game to avoid picking up a large pile of cards when the deck is empty. Intermediate: Teamwork: If you are the attacker, lead ranks that your partner (another attacker) can follow up with, to overwhelm the defender. Advanced: Card Counting: Essential in a 32ndcard deck. Know which Queens (Overs) and Kings have been discarded to gauge when your 10s or 9s become safe beats. - Tip: Avoid 'dirtying' your hand by picking up too many suit cards early. - Tip: In Secret Dudák, revealing your trump suit too early gives opponents an advantage in planning their attacks.",
    "variations": "- Open Dudák (Otevřený Dudák): Each player's trump suit is decided in advance and known to all; rules after trumps declared apply throughout. - Pocket Dudák (Kapsičkový Dudák): Each player is dealt a hand plus a face-down trump card; trumps are revealed when the player declares. - Secret Dudák (Tajný Dudák): Like Pocket Dudák except no one may see others' trump cards until the owner declares and turns the card face up. - Dudák with a Talon (Lízaný Dudák): Not all cards are dealt; remainder forms a talon. Players draw to replenish hand after play; when talon is empty, play continues as standard Dudák."
