    "history": "Originating in Indonesia as a social card game, Empat Satu is widely played in coffee shops and community gatherings. Its simplicity makes it accessible across all age groups. - Mid-20th Century: Becomes a staple Indonesian leisure game. - Modern Era: Digital versions and mobile apps bring the game to a global audience. Derived from simpler matching games, it evolved to include a unique 'penalty' scoring system for hands with mixed suits. Often played for small stakes or as a quick social filler between longer games.",
