    "setup": "Players: Any number of players can bet against a single Banker. Traditionally 1-10 players. Deck: Standard 52-card deck. Card ranks: Ace (low) through King (high). Equipment: 1. **Dealing Box**: Special box with a slot to expose card faces while preventing double-dealing. 2. **Layout**: Pasteboard or cloth with 13 card ranks (Ace through King) where players place bets. 3. **Case Keeper**: An abacus-like device with beads to track which cards have been drawn from the deck. 4. **Coppers**: Hexagonal tokens placed on bets to indicate 'losing' prediction. Dealing: Dealer (the Banker) shuffles the deck and places it in the dealing box. The first card exposed (the 'Soda') is a dead card and is removed from play. Betting then begins.",
    "rules": "Objective: Wager on whether a specific card rank will be the next 'Winner' or 'Loser' card drawn from the dealing box. Gameplay: 1. **Betting Phase**: Players place chips on any card rank on the layout, indicating a bet that card will 'Win' (be drawn as the second card in a turn). 2. **The Draw**: Dealer exposes two cards from the box in sequence. 3. **Card 1 (Loser)**: The first card is the LOSER. The House collects all bets on that rank (unless 'coppering' was used). 4. **Card 2 (Winner)**: The second card is the WINNER. The House pays 1:1 on all bets on that rank. 5. **Next Turn**: Betting resumes for the next pair of cards. The game continues until the deck is exhausted. Scoring: Betting outcomes determined by card draws. House profits from splits only. - **Soda**: The first card of the entire deck (removed before play begins; not part of gameplay). - **Hock**: The last card...",
