    "rules": "Objective: Assemble a 5-card hand of the same suit that totals exactly or as close to 51 as possible. Gameplay: Each turn (clockwise), a player MUST perform one of the following exchanges with the table: 1. 1-for-1: Swap one card from your hand for one card from the table. 2. 5-for-5: Swap your entire hand for all five cards on the table. 3. Stop: If you have a high score (usually 40+), you may say 'Stop'. This triggers the final round. Scoring: Collect 5 cards of same suit totaling as close to 51 as possible. Ace=11, K/Q/J=10, 2-10=face value. Exact 51 = instant win. - Matching Suit constraint: Your score is only the total of cards within the SAME suit. If you have cards of different suits, you only count the suit that gives you the highest total. - Empty Market: If a 5-for-5 swap occurs, the next player may choose to 'Refresh the Market' by clearing the discarded hand and dealing...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Identify the 'Power Suits' on the table. If you see the Ace of Hearts on the table, immediately start collecting Hearts. Intermediate: The 'Stop' Timing: Don't wait for 51. If you hit 45 or 48 early in the game, call 'Stop' immediately. Your opponents will likely have fragmented hands and won't be able to catch up in a single turn. Advanced: Market Manipulation: If you have a card that an opponent clearly needs (e.g., they are swapping for Spades and you hold the Spade King), keep it in your hand as long as possible. Only drop it to the table when you can simultaneously pick up a card that completes your own suit. - Tip: Keep track of which suits other players are taking. If two people are collecting Diamonds, switch to Clubs or Spades to avoid competition. - Tip: A 5-for-5 swap is a great way to 'reset' a bad hand if the table has even two cards of a matching suit.",
