    "strategy": "Basic: Keep track of the four Over-Knaves. If you hold the 'Acorn' Over-Knave, you have the absolute highest card in the gameâ€”save it to capture an opponent's Ace or Ten. Intermediate: The Tenth Order: Because Tens are worth exactly as much as Aces (1 point), treat them with equal value. Throwing a Ten on your partner's winning trick is a common and necessary strategy. Advanced: Void-Forcing: If you know an opponent is void in a suit, lead that suit repeatedly to force them to use up their high trumps (Over-Knaves) early, 'cleaning out' the defense for your Aces later in the game. - Tip: In the first few tricks, try to extract the Over-Knaves from the opponents to see where the power lies. - Tip: If your partner leads an Ace, throw your Ten of that suit on top of it immediately to secure the points.",
