    "strategy": "Basic: Prioritize matching the ends for Bergenndstyle points. The dice bonuses are great, but the points for double-matching (2 or 3 points) are the foundation of a win. Intermediate: Scorpion Sabotage: If you can track which player is short on tiles, try to lead a number that forces them to play a Scorpion tile, hitting them with penalty points just as they think they are about to domino. Advanced: Freezing the Oasis: If you have a strong lead, try to play tiles that force opponents to draw heavily from the Oasis. Once it's empty, you can 'block' the game if you have the lowest remaining pips. - Tip: Hold the Flower tile as long as possible. If you can end the round by playing it on a matching end, you maximize your score in a single turn. - Tip: Blanks are your safest cardsâ€”they can never be the Flower or the Scorpion (since dice only have 1-6).",
