    "strategy": "Basic: Protect your high trumps. Since the 5 and Jack are so powerful, don't waste them on a trick you can win with a lower card. Use them to 'pull' trumps from your opponents. Intermediate: The Ace of Hearts is your wildcard. Never forget that it is a trump. It can be a devastating surprise if your opponent leads a suit they think you are void in, only for you to 'Ace' them. Advanced: Black Suit Logic: Remember that in black suits (Spades/Clubs), the 2 is higher than the 10. This frequently trips up beginners. Use your low-number black cards to win non-trump tricks. - Tip: Rob the trump whenever possible. Getting that extra high card is often the difference between winning 2 tricks and winning 3. - Tip: In partnerships, if your partner wins the first two tricks, 'throw' your best cards to help them secure the third trick and the round.",
