    "history": "Garrafina developed in Spanish domino circles as a trains-family game related to Mexican Train but with stricter ownership rules for each player's branch. - 20th century: Popularized in Spanish social domino play. - 2000s onward: Online platforms such as Ludoteka helped standardize three- and four-player procedures. Core play remained stable while table rules varied on session length, tie handling in blocked hands, and two- or three-player exchange procedures. Garrafina is common in Spanish-language domino communities and often played as a multi-deal score session.",
