    "history": "First English rules were published in August 2011 from a report by Alexey Lobashev, who learned the game from Takam Ludovic Thierry; a corrected version was published in August 2012 after clarifying misunderstood trick and pickup rules. The game is a popular family game in Cameroon. - 2011: First English rules publication based on local player report. - 2012: Corrected version published with clarified trick and pickup procedures. - Present: Continues in informal family and social play. Published corrections focused on exact trick interruption and pickup behavior when a player cannot or does not follow suit. Generala functions as a social elimination series where a champion emerges after repeated games.",
