    "rules": "Objective: Empty your hand first so your team scores the value of your final attack tile and reaches game target before opponents. Gameplay: Dealer leads by placing one covered tile and one face-up attack tile. On each subsequent turn, a player may pass or respond by playing a matching tile (or a king except against lance/pawn), then immediately plays a new attack tile. If three consecutive players pass, the last successful attacker leads again with a covered tile and any new attack. Players always act by either playing two tiles or passing. The deal ends when a player plays their final pair. Scoring: Winning team scores the point value of the winner's final attack tile; some finishes after triple-pass allow doubled value when final pair is equal. - Kings can substitute only against non-lance and non-pawn attacks. - Passing is always allowed, even when a legal response exists. - A king...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Preserve kings for difficult defenses and key tempo swings after pass chains. Intermediate: Use passes to keep partnership tempo and avoid feeding opponents favorable attack values. Advanced: Track exposed piece counts and concealed lead cards to infer hidden hand structure and endgame outs. - Tip: Because action is pass or two-tile play, parity of hand size and expected response windows matters. - Tip: Coordinate implicitly with partner through attack choice; you cannot communicate explicitly.",
