    "history": "Haitian Dominoes is part of Caribbean partnership domino traditions and is documented as a mainstream social game in Haiti. - Traditional era: Partnership dominoes become a staple social game in Haiti. - Modern era: Standardized scoring terms such as Dekabes become widely documented. - Current play: Home, street, and tournament variants continue with regional scoring differences. The core structure stayed stable: anti-clockwise partnership play, blocked-round tie handling, and streak-based victory instead of long additive totals. Table gestures between partners are commonly used in casual play, though some organized formats ban gestures.",
