    "history": "Originating in South Asia, Hazari is closely related to the British game 'Crash' (or Thirteen-card Brag). It has become the most popular card game in Bangladesh, often played in tea stalls and social clubs. - Mid-20th Century: Hazari evolves from 13-card Brag variants in colonial Bengal. - 1971-Present: Becomes a cultural staple in independent Bangladesh. - Modern Era: Digital versions thrive among the Bangladeshi diaspora. The game standardized the 10-point value for all high cards (10 through Ace), simplifying the mental math of its 1000-point target. Typically played with a distinct Bangladeshi fervor, often involves 'calling' your sets loudly when ready.",
