    "history": "Hearts appeared in the USA in the 1880s, based on earlier evasion games from Europe such as Reversis and Polignac. - 1880s: Hearts first documented in American game books. - 1909: The Queen of Spades ('Black Lady') standardly included as a 13-point penalty card. - 1990s: Becomes a global phenomenon after being included in Microsoft Windows 3.1. - Present: One of the most played card games online and in Windows. Originally a simple game of avoiding hearts, it evolved to include the high penalty of the Queen of Spades and the 'Shoot the Moon' reversal rule. Known worldwide due to its inclusion in early Windows operating systems. One of the most recognizable card games globally.",
