    "overview": "Hindersche (meaning 'Backwards') is a rare and traditional reverse trick-taking game played exclusively in the central Black Forest of Germany. It is an Ace-Ten game where the objective is to *avoid* taking tricks containing card points. It is noted for its antiquity, using a 36-card pack and being played anticlockwise. Origin: Germany (Black Forest) Players: 4 Deck: 36-card German-suited deck (Schafkopf/Jass deck) Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 30-45 minutes",
