    "setup": "Players: 2 players (opposing teams). Deck: Standard 52-card deck. No Jokers. Equipment: Standard 52-card deck. Pencil and paper optional for keeping score. Dealing: A match consists of three 'periods'. In each period, the entire 52-card deck is dealt in batches of 5 cards per player. The final deal of the period is 6 cards each.",
    "rules": "Objective: Score more 'goals' than your opponent over three periods of play. Gameplay: 1. Players alternate playing one card face up to a central pile. 2. **Breakaway**: You create a breakaway if you play a card of the SAME rank as the card currently on top of the pile, OR if you play any **Jack**. 3. **Scoring a Goal**: Once you have a breakaway, you score a goal if you match the NEXT card played by your opponent. 4. **Defense/Saves**: If your opponent creates a breakaway, your current breakaway is cancelled. You can also 'save' a goal attempt by playing a card that your opponent cannot match. Scoring: Players score goals by creating breakaways and matching opponent cards. Three periods of play (or sudden death overtime if tied). - Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hockey. - Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Players score goals by creating...",
