    "description": "Hyakunin Isshu (ç™¾äººä¸€é¦– - 'One Hundred People, One Poem Each') is a traditional Japanese card game based on a classical anthology of waka poems. It is played as a competitive game called 'Karuta'. Players must match a poem being read aloud with the...",
