    "history": "Baccarat was introduced to Indonesia via international trade and colonial influence. It became a staple in private clubs and regulated casinos (when they were operational). - 19th Century: Baccarat enters Asian maritime trade hubs. - 20th Century: Popularized in regional gambling centers like Jakarta and Batam. - Present: Played primarily in private social clubs and online platforms. Indonesian play often follows 'Punto Banco' rules, with occasional local variations in tie-payouts and specific 'side bets' unique to Southeast Asian bank games. The game is associated with high-stakes social environments and prestige.",
