    "setup": "Players: Standard with 4-5 players. Deck: Two standard decks and four Jokers (Total 108 cards). Equipment: 108 cards, score sheet, chips for stakes (optional) Dealing: Varies by round: Hand 1 (9 cards), Hand 2 (10), ... Hand 9 (16 cards).",
    "rules": "Objective: Be the first to 'Go Out' by melding all cards in your hand and have the lowest total score after 9 hands. Gameplay: 1. **Contracts**: Each hand has a specific contract to fulfill before melding. 2. **The Call**: Any player can call for a discard out of turn. If accepted, they must take the discard PLUS a penalty card from the stock. (Limit: 3 calls per hand). 3. **Melds**: Threes (sets) and Fours (runs). Jokers are wild. 4. **Pointing**: Jokers (25), Black Aces (15), K-Q-J-10 (10), 2-9 (Face), Red Aces (1). Lowest total wins. Scoring: Winner scores 0 for the hand. Other players score penalty points for cards remaining in hand. - Hand 1: 3 Threes (Sets) - Hand 2: 2 Threes, 1 Four (Run) - Hand 3: 2 Fours, 1 Three - Hand 4: 3 Fours - Hand 5: 4 Threes - Hand 6: 3 Threes, 1 Four - Hand 7: 2 Threes, 2 Fours - Hand 8: 1 Three, 3 Fours - Hand 9: 4 Fours - The Call: Take discard out...",
