    "strategy": "Basic: With multiple sets, it is much easier to find an identical 'Eye'. Focus on the 'Sum-Pairs' first, as they determine the flow of your hand. Intermediate: Hoarding: If you see that 6-6 tiles are appearing frequently in discards, start hoarding 4-4 or 3-1 to complete 10/20 sums. The Big game is about recognizing high-volume numbers. Advanced: Defensive Discarding: Observe the 'Sum' your neighbors are building. If your neighbor is picking up low-value tiles (1s and 2s), don't discard any 8s or 9s—you are likely giving them their 10-sum. - Tip: The 4-2 tile is extremely powerful in the Big variant because it can bridge both 10 and 20 target sums depending on whether you count it as 6 or 3. - Tip: Don't wait for a 'Three Nobles' combination unless you have 3/4 of the pieces; it's too slow for this fast variant.",
