    "overview": "Katti (meaning 'cut' or 'bundle' in some dialects) is a traditional Indian banking and gambling game of pure chance, closely related to Andar Bahar. Originating in South India (Karnataka and Tamil Nadu), the game involves betting on which of two piles ('Andar'/Inside or 'Bahar'/Outside) will first receive a card matching the rank of a central 'House' card. It is a staple of festival gambling and modern online casinos. Origin: India (Karnataka/Tamil Nadu) Players: 1 dealer + unlimited bettors Deck: Standard 52-card deck Difficulty: Beginner Duration: 1-5 minutes per round",
