    "history": "Dates to the early 20th century in Western Europe. It evolved from simpler 'penalty' games like Hearts into a structured multi-round tournament format favored by university students and social clubs. - 1920s: King spreads in French-speaking card clubs. - 1970s: The game is exported to the UK and USA as 'Barbu'. - Present: A very common social game in Flanders and Francophone Belgium. - Modern: Digital versions like 'Kingen.be' maintain a competitive player base. The game's variety (changing rules every round) makes it more dynamic than Bridge while retaining significant strategic depth. In Belgium, it is a staple of 'cafÃ© culture' and social gatherings.",
