    "rules": "Objective: Score more points than the opposing team through tricks and melds. The contractor team must outscore the defenders. Gameplay: Must follow suit. If unable, MUST trump if possible. Trick-winning is counter-clockwise. Scoring: Card points from tricks (161 total) plus last trick (10); melds (terc, kvart, sequences, four of a kind, bella) added. Contractor team must outscore defenders or defenders score all. First to 501 wins the game. - Follow suit if possible; if unable, must trump if possible; otherwise play any card. - Player to dealer's right leads first; play is anticlockwise. - Bidding decides trump and contractor team; contractor must outscore defenders. - Melds (sequences, sets, bella) declared before first trick; only highest small meld counts per team, bella always scores. - Last trick worth 10 extra points; total card points 161. First to 501 wins the game. Win...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Partnership Communication: Only the highest meld declaration at the table counts for that point category. Communicate with your partner to ensure your team's best meld is prioritized. Intermediate: The 'Nine' Strategy: If your partner bids (takes), and you hold the Nine of trumps (Nell), try to lead it as early as possible if you suspect the opponent holds the Over-knave (Jass). Advanced: Defensive Ducking: If your team is the defender, don't always trump in. Sometimes it's better to lose a trick to save a high card for the 'Last Trick' (10 points). - Tip: Always declare your melds before the first trick is played! Late declarations are usually void. - Tip: In the Gourds (TÃ¶k) suit, the cards can look similar; double-check your 'Over' and 'Under' knaves.",
    "variations": "- Kontra / Rekontra / Szubkontra: Before play, defenders may say kontra to double hand score; contractor may rekontra; defenders may szubkontra (8×). Does not apply on throw-in hands. - Throw-in melds: If any player holds a meld worth 100+ points (four of a kind or sequence of 5+), they must declare; hand is thrown in and meld points scored. Concealment penalized: opponents score 161. - Maccs (double game): If a team reaches 501 when opponents have less than 251, winners score a double game (maccs)."
