    "setup": "Players: 2 to 4 players individually. Deck: Standard 52-card deck. **Special Capture Values**: 10 of Diamonds = 16, 2 of Spades = 15, Aces = 14 or 1. Equipment: Standard 52-card deck. **Special Capture Values**: 10 of Diamonds = 16, 2 of Spades = 15, Aces = 14 or 1. Dealing: Each player receives 4 cards; 4 cards are placed face-up on the table. The rest form a draw pile.",
    "rules": "Objective: Score as few points as possible. The round ends when a player hits 13 or 21 penalty points. Gameplay: 1. **Forced Capture**: If you hold a card that CAN capture a card or sum from the table, you MUST capture it. You cannot choose to discard if a capture is possible. 2. **Building**: You can 'build' onto table cards to avoid a current capture, but you must be able to capture the build yourself on a future turn. 3. **Table Clearing (Tabbe)**: Clearing the table is worth -1 point (a good thing in misere). Scoring: Score as few points as possible. Game ends when a player reaches 13 or 21 penalty points. - Forced capture rule: must capture if possible - 10 of Diamonds (Storan) = 2 penalty points - 2 of Spades (Lillan) = 1 penalty point - Each Ace = 1 penalty point - Most Cards = 1 penalty point - Most Spades = 1 penalty point - Tabbe (clearing table) = -1 point Win condition:...",
