    "strategy": "Basic: Keep at least one Trump card in reserve (especially the Ace). This is your 'Get out of jail free' card. If you are forced to beat a high card, the Ace guarantees you can move the turn to your opponent. Intermediate: Pile Management: If the pile is small, intentionally pick up a low plain card rather than using a high card to beat it. This keeps your hand count low and preserves your power cards for when the pile gets dangerous. Advanced: The 'Nakladka' Trap: Bait your opponent into winning a small trick, then use your 'piling up' card to play a mid-range Trump. This forces them into a high-risk situation where they might have to pick up 3 cards, including the trump you just played. - Tip: In the 2-player game, memory of the Trumps is fairly easy. Track the 'Ace of Trumps' constantlyâ€”it is the game-winner. - Tip: Discard your 6s and 7s of non-trump suits as quickly as possible...",
