    "strategy": "Basic: Prioritize the Aces. Holding two Aces in a 6-card hand makes you nearly guaranteed to capture at least 10 points. If your partner also holds an Ace, you have 20 pointsâ€”just one point shy of winning the round. Intermediate: Trump Defensive: If the opponent chooses trumps, lead low cards in your 'longest' suit to force them to use their trump cards early. If you can exhaust their 6 trump cards, your remaining Aces becomes masters. Advanced: The 'Kapot' Strategy: If your team has high cards in all suits, aim for 'Kapot' (winning all 6 tricks). This erases multiple branches (usually 2 or 3) and is the fastest path to victory. - Tip: Always watch which player 'Accepted' the Trump. They are the target for all your defensive leads. - Tip: In Kujong, the Queen of Spades (De Mit) is the 'Joker' of the deckâ€”don't lose her to a low Jack.",
