    "rules": "Objective: Win more tricks than either of the other two players individually. Gameplay: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. Highest Matador wins any trick, followed by other trumps, then high cards of led suit. 3. **Puesta**: If the Hombre doesn't win more tricks than one opponent, they 'lose' and must pay the pot. Scoring: Win more tricks than either of the other two players individually. - Must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. - In game contracts, Spadille (A of spades) and Basta (A of clubs) are permanent trumps; Manille is second highest (2 in black trumps, 7 in red). - Matadors have limited follow-suit exemptions: when a trump is led, you need not play a matador unless a higher matador was led and you have no other trumps. - Declarer wins by taking more tricks than either defender; nolo contracts: declarer must take no tricks. Win condition: Win more tricks...",
