    "history": "Developed in American home poker games as a variant of Seven Card Stud to increase pot sizes and the frequency of big hands (Quads/Straight Flushes). - 1950s: Becomes a popular 'Dealer's Choice' filler game. - 1970s: Reaches the fringes of underground casino play. - Present: Commonly played in low-stakes social games and online 'wild card' lobbies. The game evolved into several sub-variants, including 'Hi-Lo' and 'Follow the Queen', but the core 'Low Hole' remains the most mathematically straightforward. Known as a 'beginner killer' because the presence of wild cards masks the true strength of opponents' hands.",
