    "strategy": "Basic: Count points, not tricks. Aces and Tens are the valuable cards. Don't waste your high trumps on low-value tricks. Intermediate: Trump Management: In a suit game, you have 11 trumps. Use them to capture opponents' Aces and Tens, but don't exhaust them too early. Advanced: Void Creation: If you are declarer and have a weak suit, try to void yourself in that suit early so you can trump opponents' leads. - Tip: The Ten is the second-highest card in point value but ranks low in trick-taking power. - Tip: Schneider (91+ points) doubles the game value. Play for it if your hand is strong. - Tip: Watch for opponents playing high non-trump cards earlyâ€”they may be voiding a suit.",
