    "strategy": "Basic: Don't 'dump' your easiest cards early. If you see a way to play a 7 of Hearts, wait until you have another card that depends on it. The more cards you put on the table, the more options your OPPONENTS have on their turns. Intermediate: The Big Reveal: Wait until you can play 4-5 cards at once by rearranging the whole board. This 'explodes' your hand and often ends the game before opponents can react to the new board state. Advanced: Defensive Manipulation: If you see an opponent looking for a 5 of Spades to finish their sequence, and that 5 is already in a 'Set of 5s' on the table, try to move that 5 into a DIFFERENT sequence that is harder for them to access. - Tip: Sequences are better for manipulation than Sets. A sequence of 3-4-5-6 can be split into two 3-card melds if you have the right cards; a 3-card Set is 'atomic' and cannot be split. - Tip: Always scan for 'orphan'...",
    "variations": "- Machiavelli with Jokers: Increases speed but reduces late-game logic complexity. - Rummikub: The tile-based equivalent. - Vatikan: A German variant with similar manipulation rules."
