    "setup": "Players: 4 players in two partnerships. Deck: 40 cards: Suits are Oros (Coins), Copas (Cups), Espadas (Swords), Bastos (Clubs). Equipment: 40 cards: Suits are Oros (Coins), Copas (Cups), Espadas (Swords), Bastos (Clubs). Dealing: Each player receives 10 cards. The dealer flips the last card to determine the Trump suit.",
    "rules": "Objective: Your partnership must win tricks containing the high-value point cards (Seven=5, Ace=4, King=3, Horse=2, Jack=1) plus one point per trick, and be the first team to reach 35 or more cumulative points to win the game. Gameplay: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. Must try to win the trick if possible (Overtake). 3. If unable to follow suit, you must play a trump card if you have one. 4. The winner of the trick leads the next. Scoring: Card points (Seven=5, Ace=4, King=3, Horse=2, Jack=1) plus one point per trick won (la negra). Total 70 points per deal. Team with more than 35 scores the difference; first to 35 cumulative wins. - Must follow suit if possible. - If an opponent is winning the trick, must beat their card if able (subject to follow suit). - When unable to follow suit, must play a trump if you have one. - Cannot discard a seven of a non-trump suit until that suit...",
