    "history": "A member of the Cyprus family of domino games, named after the distinctive Maltese Cross pattern formed by the tableau during play. - Traditional: Played in Mediterranean regions with double-six domino sets - Modern: Remains popular as a family domino game - Present: Played worldwide as a classic domino variant The game can be adapted for larger domino sets (double-9, double-12) by adjusting the matching rules accordingly. A social family game commonly played in Cyprus and Mediterranean regions.",
    "setup": "Players: 2-4 players, individually or in partnerships Deck: Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles). For 2 players: 7 tiles each. For 3-4 players: 5-6 tiles each. Equipment: Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles). For 2 players: 7 tiles each. For 3-4 players: 5-6 tiles each. Dealing: Tiles are dealt evenly. Remaining tiles form the boneyard.",
