    "strategy": "Basic: Try to win early tricks so you can declare trumps if you have a marriage. The first marriage declaration is crucial as it sets trumps for the whole hand. Intermediate: Decide whether to declare your own marriage or ask partner. Declaring yourself gives 2 points and sets trumps immediately. Asking partner can be safer but 'breaks' your own marriages. Track which marriages have been 'broken'. Advanced: The 'half marriage' declaration can be a clever tactic - it breaks all marriages in both hands, preventing opponents from declaring trumps later. Timing when to declare is key: too early and opponents know the trump suit; too late and opponent might declare first. - Tip: If you have multiple marriages, you might declare a non-trump one first (if you can win another trick) for the extra game point - Tip: The last trick is worth 1 game point - fight for it, especially in close games -...",
