    "history": "Minchiate was invented in Florence in the 16th century. The name comes from 'sminchiare' meaning 'to play a high trump', though some incorrectly associate it with vulgar meanings. The alternative name 'Germini' derives from Gemini (trump 35). - 16th Century: Invented in Florence - 17th Century: Spreads to Rome, Sicily, and Genoa - 18th-19th Century: Highly popular and respected game throughout Italy - 1930s: Effectively dies out as last card manufacturer stops production - Late 20th Century: Reproduction decks created for collectors - Present: Played by enthusiasts attempting to revive the game The game evolved from standard Tarocchi by adding 19 extra trumps (virtues, elements, zodiac signs) to create a 97-card deck. Considered one of the most sophisticated card games of its era. Played by nobility and intellectuals. The complexity of the game reflected the cultural sophistication of...",
