    "strategy": "Basic: Find the 8-Card Fit. If you and your partner have 8 or more cards combined in Spades or Hearts (the Major suits), that should almost always be your trump suit. If no 8-card fit exists, 'No Trumps' is often the best choice if you have balanced strength. Intermediate: Counting Losers: Before playing the first card from the dummy, count how many tricks you are likely to lose in each suit. If you have 3 losers in Hearts, you must find a way to 'Trump' those losers in the dummy or discard them on long side-suits. Advanced: Defensive Lead: As the defender (opponent of the declarer), try to lead a suit where the declarer/dummy looks weakest. If the dummy has no high Diamonds, lead a Diamond into the declarer's potential weakness. - Tip: If your combined HCP is 20-25, aim for a 'Part-score' (7 tricks). If you have 26+, aim for 'Game' for a bigger bonus. - Tip: Always draw the opponents'...",
