    "strategy": "Basic: Pay attention to the top card of the play pile. React quickly to matching cards. Manage your money cards wisely - don't use high-value cards to buy small numbers of cards. Intermediate: Track which cards have been played to predict what might come up. Time your buying to get the best value from your money cards. Force your opponent to use their high-value money cards early. Advanced: Card counting is possible with practice. Optimize your money exchanges to preserve valuable cards. Use the speed factor to your advantage - play quickly when you know a match is unlikely. - Tip: Kings are most efficient for buying (5 cards each) - Tip: Don't waste a Queen (15 cards) to buy fewer than 15 cards - Tip: Watch your opponent's money area to know what they can buy - Tip: Capturing large piles can give you many cards at once - Tip: Speed is key - practice recognizing matches instantly",
