    "history": "Mpourloto is derived from French Belote, which spread throughout Europe in the 20th century. The Greek variant developed its own scoring and meld rules, distinguishing it from the French original. - Early 20th Century: Belote spreads to Greece - Mid-20th Century: Greek rules formalize with unique scoring - Present: Popular in Greece and among Greek communities abroad The key differences from Belote include: different meld values, all melds count (not just the highest), the 'mesa' rule for failed contracts, and the ability to choose any suit in the second bidding round. A popular social game in Greece, played in cafes (kafeneia), homes, and clubs. The game is part of the Greek card-playing tradition alongside games like Prefa and Biriba.",
