    "rules": "Objective: Be the first partnership to reach 1000 points by winning tricks, capturing valuable cards, and declaring melds. Gameplay: Player left of dealer leads. Must follow suit if possible. If unable, must play a trump. Must beat the highest card played so far if possible (overtaking is compulsory). Scoring: Points from melds, card values, and bonuses. Target is 1000 points. - Jack and 9 of trumps are highest cards - All melds count toward score - Must follow suit, must trump if void - Must overtake if possible - Mesa: failed contract gives all points to opponents Win condition: First partnership to reach 1000 points wins.",
    "strategy": "Basic: Bid with strong hands, especially with good trump support. Declare all melds. Try to capture the trump Jack and 9. Intermediate: Consider the Mesa risk when bidding - a failed contract is devastating. Coordinate with partner through card play. Save high trumps for important tricks. Advanced: Card counting is essential. Track trumps and high cards. Understand when to sacrifice a trick to set up future wins. Master the compulsory overtaking rules. - Tip: The trump Jack (20 points) is the most valuable single card - Tip: Don't bid unless you have strong trump support or a good meld - Tip: Mesa can swing hundreds of points - bid carefully - Tip: Sequences are valuable - look for consecutive cards in the same suit - Tip: The King-Queen of trumps (Mpourloto) gives a 20-point meld",
