    "rules": "Objective: Be first team to 100 points (or agreed target). Score by going out or by having fewer pips when blocked. Gameplay: 1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant. Scoring: Winners score losers' unplayed pips. Blocked: lower pip total wins. Tie = no score (or variant rules). - All 28 tiles dealt; 7 each. - Play counter-clockwise (or clockwise per locale). - Must play if possible; pass when blocked. - Blocked: lower pip total wins. -...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Play to empty hand. Block opponents when possible. Intermediate: Track played tiles. Coordinate with partner via play. Advanced: Force blocks; manage pip count in blocked hands. - Tip: Save doubles for blocking. - Tip: Track which numbers are exhausted. - Tip: In blocked games, low pip count matters.",
