    "overview": "Pass the Trash is a stud poker variant in which each player receives seven cards, posts antes, and after a betting round passes three unwanted cards to the next active player to the left. After a second betting round players discard two cards, order the remaining five face down, then reveal them one at a time with betting between each reveal. The highest five-card hand at showdown wins the pot. Origin: USA Players: 2-7 Deck: Standard 52-card deck Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 15-30 minutes",
    "history": "Country/Region of Origin: USA Time Period: Early 1900s Historical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region Cultural Significance: Popular social and family game - Early 1900s: Game first documented - Mid 1900s: Spread to other regions - Modern Era: Continues to be played worldwide - Online Presence: Digital versions available",
    "setup": "Players: 2 to 7 players. Best with 4. No partnerships. Deck: Standard 52-card deck. One deck. No jokers. Equipment: Standard 52-card deck, poker chips for antes and betting. Dealing: After antes are placed, seven cards are dealt face down to each player. Dealing is clockwise.",
    "rules": "Objective: Win the pot by having the highest five-card poker hand at showdown after the pass, discard, and reveal phases. Gameplay: 1. Antes: All players post the ante. 2. Deal: Seven cards face down to each player. 3. First betting round: Player to dealer's left acts first. 4. Pass the trash: Each active player places three unwanted cards face down; when all are ready, each set of three is passed to the next active player to the left. 5. Second betting round. 6. Discard: Everyone discards two unwanted cards (each keeps five). 7. Arrange: Each player chooses an order for the five cards and stacks them face down. 8. Reveal and bet: Each player turns over the first card of their stack; betting round begun by the player with the highest hand showing. Repeat for second, third, and fourth cards (four cards face up, one face down). 9. Final betting round. 10. Showdown: Highest five-card hand...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Pass your three worst cards in the first pass; avoid keeping unconnected high cards. Discard the two that least help your five-card hand. Intermediate: Track which cards you passed and to whom; infer what neighbours might have. Order your five cards to reveal strong cards early to lead betting when you have the high hand showing. Advanced: Bluff by passing strong cards to mislead the left neighbour; balance between improving your hand and hiding strength. In high-low variants, decide declaration based on passed and received cards. - Tip: Position to dealer's left acts first in the first betting round; use it to apply pressure. - Tip: When revealing, leading with a pair or high card can win the betting round or build the pot when you have the best hand.",
    "variations": "- High-Low: Before showdown everyone declares high, low, or both (e.g. chips in fist); high and low winners split the pot. - Three-phase pass: First phase: three cards passed left. Second: two cards passed two places left. Third: one card passed three places left. Betting round after each phase. - Pot split with next right: Pot is split between the high hand and the next active player to the right (the one who received your passed cards)."
