    "overview": "Pick a Partner is a stud poker variant for an even number of players. Everyone antes and receives five cards face down. All players simultaneously expose one card (roll). The highest card holder picks a partner; then the highest unpartnered player picks, until all are paired. Each partnership combines their eight remaining cards and selects three to use with their two upcards to form a five-card hand. Three betting rounds follow, with one of the three chosen cards turned face up after each round. Partners bet as individuals; the team with the best hand shares the pot, or one partner wins the whole pot if the other folded. Origin: USA Players: 2-6 Deck: Standard 52-card deck. Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 20-40 minutes",
