    "rules": "Objective: Score 57 or more points from a pool of 114 available points. Gameplay: Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game. Scoring: Score 57 or more points from a pool of 114 available points. - Follow suit if possible; if void in suit...",
