    "setup": "Players: 4 or 6 players in partnerships. Deck: Standard 52-card deck plus two distinguishable jokers. Off-Jack = Jack of same color as trump Jack. Equipment: Standard deck, 2 jokers, score sheet. Dealing: 4 players: 9 cards each. 6 players: 8 cards each. Remaining cards form widow.",
    "rules": "Objective: Be the first partnership to reach 21 points by capturing scoring cards in tricks. Gameplay: 1. Deal 9 (4p) or 8 (6p) cards each. 2. Bid 2-10 (or 2-7 without trey). Dealer cannot steal the bid. 3. Bidder declares trump. 4. Discard and draw to 6 cards. 5. Play: bidder leads. Follow suit or trump. 6. Score: High, Low, Jack, Off-Jack, Jokers, Game (1 each); Trey 3 (optional). First to 21 wins. Scoring: Points from High, Low, Jack, Off-Jack, Jokers, Game, Trey (optional). Bid and make to score; set = lose bid. - Trump order: A, K, Q, J, Off-Jack, High Joker, Low Joker, 10-2. - Low = held by team (lowest trump in play). - Bid and make: score points. Set: lose bid, opponents score. - Win only when reaching 21+ on a hand where you made your bid. Win condition: First team to 21, on a hand where they made their bid.",
    "strategy": "Basic: Count trumps; bid conservatively. Protect Off-Jack and jokers. Intermediate: Use discard phase to load trumps. Lead trump to draw high cards. Advanced: Track scoring cards played. Coordinate with partner. - Tip: Widow (6p) gives bidder flexibility. - Tip: Low is scored by who holds itâ€”ducking can save Low.",
