    "rules": "Objective: Form a hand whose total value is as near as possible to 21 without going over; beat the banker. Best hand is Pontoon (Ace plus ten-value card in two cards), then Five Card Trick (five cards totaling 21 or less), then 21 in three or four cards; hands over 21 are bust. Banker wins ties. Gameplay: 1. Setup: One player is banker (first banker chosen at random). Banker deals one card face down to each player; players other than banker look at their card and place initial bets within agreed min and max. Banker deals a second card face down to each. If banker has Pontoon, banker collects double from each and hand ends. 2. Players' turns: From dealer's left, each player may declare Pontoon (A-J/10), split equal ranks (extra bet, two hands), buy a card (add to stake, card face down), twist (no extra stake, card face up), or stick (total at least 15). Once a player has twisted, they...",
