    "overview": "Pyramide (The Pyramid) is a popular French social card game, often played in festive or party settings. It is a game of memory, deduction, and high-stakes bluffing. Players are dealt a private hand of cards which they must mÃ©morise and then place face-down. A central 'Pyramid' of cards is then revealed layer-by-layer. If a player claims to have a card matching a revealed one, they can penalize an opponentâ€”but if they're caught bluffing, the penalty is doubled. It is a game of 'Who can keep a poker face while forgetting their own hand?' Origin: France Players: 3-10 Deck: Standard 52-card deck Difficulty: Beginner Duration: 10-15 minutes",
