    "overview": "Quartett is a German and Austrian matching game where players collect complete quartets (families of four cards) by asking others for specific cards. You must hold at least one card of the quartet to ask. If the asked player has it, they give it and you continue; if not, they say 'not at home' and their turn begins. Origin: Germany / Austria (from British Happy Families, mid-19th century) Players: 2-6 (optimal 3-4) Deck: 32-card German (or dedicated Quartett pack) Difficulty: Beginner Duration: 10-25 minutes",
