    "overview": "Ramino Pokerato is an Italian Rummy game that combines draw-and-discard melding with poker-style betting. Players receive 10 cards from a double deck with four Jokers; after an optional blind and betting round, play proceeds with draw from stock or discard, then discard, until a player goes out by melding 10 cards in sets and runs and discarding the 11th. Origin: Italy Players: 2-6 Deck: Double deck of 52 cards plus four Jokers (108 cards). Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 20-45 minutes",
    "history": "Ramino Pokerato is an Italian Rummy variant that combines Rummy melding with poker-style betting. The name means 'Pokerised Rummy' and applies to several Italian games; the version with Jokers and betting is described by John McLeod from Antonio de Sebastiano and others. - 20th century: Italian Rummy variant with poker-style betting documented; played in Italy and Cyprus. Multiple local variants exist with different stake rules and special-hand bonuses; contract version (Carioca) uses eight deals with different opening melds. Played in Italy and Cyprus (Pokerize variant); often played for stakes with agreed fixed blind and raises.",
    "setup": "Players: Three to five players (best); adaptable to more with extra packs. Deck: Double deck of standard 52-card packs plus four Jokers (108 cards total). Equipment: Table and chips or agreed stakes. Dealing: Dealer shuffles and is cut by player to dealer's right. Each player receives 10 cards dealt one at a time. Remainder is stacked face down as stock.",
    "rules": "Objective: Win the hand by being first to go out with 10 cards in valid sets and runs and one discard, and collect the pool; or win the betting round when all others fold. Gameplay: After the deal, the first player to dealer's left may post a blind (fare il buio). Others then call, fold, or raise in poker fashion. If two or more remain, play starts: each turn a player draws one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile, then discards one card face up. A player may go out after drawing by laying 10 cards in sets (three or more of same rank) and runs (three or more consecutive same suit; Ace may be high or low). No melds are shown until going out. Jokers are wild. The winner takes the pool. Scoring: Winner of each hand collects the pool. Special hands may entitle the winner to extra payments from active players. - Sets are three or more cards of the same rank; runs are three or...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Prioritise forming sets and runs; use Jokers to complete high-value combinations; consider folding weak hands when the blind is raised. Intermediate: Track discards to infer opponents' melds; balance going out early versus waiting for a special-hand bonus; manage bet size against hand strength. Advanced: Optimise blind and raise timing; exploit position in betting; balance immediate go-out versus drawing for a stronger closing hand. - Tip: Going out is not mandatory when possible; you may continue to try for bonus hands. - Tip: When drawing from stock, the top discard is still available to others in some variants.",
    "variations": "- Ramino Pokerato con Jolly immaginario: Played with double deck and no printed Jokers; when going out, one card in hand may be nominated as a wild card to complete one combination. - Ramino Pokerato carioca: Contract version: eight deals, each with a different opening meld requirement; 13 cards each; no poker-style betting; scoring by card values; winner of game takes game pool. - Ramino Pokerato con rilancio: Betting version with blind and raises (rilancio); same draw-discard and go-out rules as main game."
