    "history": "Round the World is a home-game poker variant in which the winning hand type rotates each deal, from high card through royal flush. It is commonly played as part of Dealer's Choice and is documented in poker variant collections. - Early 20th century: Appears in home poker circles as a rotating-hand variant. - Present: Played in Dealer's Choice and mixed poker sessions. Replaced fixed hand-ranking with a cycle of required hand types per deal. Reflects American home-game culture of varying rules per round.",
