    "history": "Tile rummy games invented by Ephraim Hertzano; conceived in 1940s Romania and later developed in Israel. Introduced to Western Europe and America; Sabra became the main version; American and International versions appear in Hertzano's 1978 Official Rummikub Book. - 1940s: Conceived in Romania by Ephraim Hertzano. - Post-WWII: Hertzano emigrated to Israel; developed and hand-made first sets. - 1978: Official Rummikub Book published (American, Sabra, International versions). - 1980: Sabra Rummikub won Spiel des Jahres.",
