    "strategy": "Basic: Get your initial 30-point meld down early so you can manipulate the table; use jokers in runs or groups you can later reclaim with the real tile. Intermediate: Break and recombine opponents' melds when it lets you play more tiles; keep runs and groups balanced so you can add from hand without getting stuck. Advanced: Plan table rearrangements before touching tiles; use time limits to pressure opponents; when pool is low, prefer melding over drawing to reduce others' options. - Tip: Place tiles from hand crosswise until your turn is complete so you can revert if you run out of time. - Tip: Joker in a group of three can be replaced by a tile of either missing color.",
