    "variations": "- Going Rummy: If you go out in one turn without having melded or laid off before, score is doubled (or +10 bonus). - No Lay-Off Until Meld: You may not lay off on others' melds until you have melded at least once. - Ace High or Low: Aces can be high (Q-K-A) or low (A-2-3). Aces then count 15 in deadwood. - Block Rummy: Discard pile is not reused. When stock runs out and next player doesn't want the discard, game ends. Lowest deadwood wins. - 500 Rummy: Multiple cards can be taken from discard; points for melds; play to 500. - Gin Rummy: Two players; knock when deadwood â‰¤10; no lay-off until knock."
