    "history": "Scarto belongs to the northern Italian tarocchi tradition and is associated with Piedmontese tarot practice. - 18th-19th century: Tarocco games spread across Piedmont. - Modern era: Scarto remains documented in tarot game references. The game keeps the broader tarocchi structure while centering tactical discard and trick control. Scarto is part of the regional Italian tarot family where local table customs shape partnership signaling and tempo.",
