    "setup": "Players: Four players in fixed partnerships; partners sit opposite each other. Play is anticlockwise. Deck: Italian 40-card pack (Latin suits: swords, clubs, cups, coins). Ranks Re, Cavallo, Fante, 7–2, A. Can use standard 52-card pack with 10s, 9s and 8s removed. Equipment: Italian 40-card deck or stripped 52-card deck; score sheet (optional). Dealing: Dealer chosen at random; deal passes right after each hand. Deal three cards to each player (anticlockwise from dealer's right), two face down to table centre, three more to each, two more to centre, three more to each. Four table cards are turned face up. If three or all four table cards are kings, redeal.",
    "rules": "Objective: Your partnership aims to score 11 or more points before the opponents by capturing cards from the table and winning scoring points (cards, coins, sette bello, prime, and sweeps). Gameplay: 1. Deal: Each player receives nine cards; four cards are placed face up on the table. 2. Play: Player to dealer's right leads; turn passes anticlockwise. Each turn a player plays one card: it may capture one or more table cards of equal rank or whose capture values sum to the played card's value; if no capture, the card stays on the table. Single-card capture takes precedence over sum capture when both apply. Captures are optional; if the card can capture, the capture must be taken. 3. End of hand: The last player to make a capture takes any remaining table cards (this does not count as a sweep). 4. Scoring: Four points per deal (majority of cards, majority of coins, sette bello, best...",
