    "variations": "- Scopone Scientifico (10-card): Ten cards dealt to each player, none to the table. Some play that the dealer's team does score one point for a sweep if the dealer's last card captures all remaining table cards. - Re bello: The king of coins (re bello) awards an extra point to the team that captures it; five points per deal (plus sweeps) instead of four. - Napola / Napoli: Team capturing A-2-3 of coins in sequence scores points equal to the highest coin in that unbroken sequence (e.g. A-2-3-4-5-6 scores 6). Capturing all ten coins (Napoleone/Cappotto) wins the game outright. - Target score 21: Some play to 21 points instead of 11, especially when using extra point variants."
