    "rules": "Objective: Soloist: Score 61+ points (in Suit/Grand) or lose no tricks (Null). Defenders: Prevent Soloist. Gameplay: Soloist can pick up the Skat (Hand game multiplier if they don't). Discard 2 cards. Declare game. Scoring: Soloist: Score 61+ points (in Suit/Grand) or lose no tricks (Null). Defenders: Prevent Soloist. - Deal 3-4-3; two cards (Skat) face-down to the table. Bidding (Reizen) determines declarer and minimum game value. - Declarer may pick up the Skat and discard two cards, or play Hand without picking up. Declare game type: Suit, Grand, or Null. - Jacks are the highest trumps (J-clubs, J-spades, J-hearts, J-diamonds). Must follow suit; may trump when void. Ten tricks; forehand leads first. - Soloist needs 61+ card points (Suit/Grand) or lose every trick (Null). Card points: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2; 9-7=0. Win condition: Soloist: Score 61+ points (in Suit/Grand) or lose...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Only bid if you have a strong hand. A good Suit hand needs 5+ trumps including top Jacks. A Grand hand needs 2-3 top Jacks and side Aces. In Null, you need 7s, 8s, 9s in every suit or voids. As a Defender, lead a suit the Soloist is likely void in (long suit) to force a trump, or lead trumps if the Soloist is weak in them (to drain them). Intermediate: The 'Short Suit' Lead: Against a Suit game, lead a short suit (singleton/doubleton) to try to ruff. But be careful not to free up the Soloist's losers. Advanced: Counting Matadors: If you have the Jack of Spades (2nd highest) but not the Jack of Clubs, you are 'Without 1'. Game Value = (1+1) * Base. If you pick up the Jack of Clubs from the Skat, you are now 'With 2' (J-Clubs, J-Spades). This changes your multiplier from 2 to 3. Be wary of overbidding if you rely on the Skat. - Tip: Jacks are always trumps in Suit/Grand. - Tip:...",
