    "rules": "Objective: The solo team (caller and optional secret partner) aims to win a majority of the 120 card points (61 or more) in tricks; the gang aims to prevent this. Gameplay: Each hand: deal all cards; then a bidding round (Pass, Solo, Solo in Hearts, Go Alone, Go Alone in Hearts) starting with the player on the lead. Each player bids once in turn; each must bid higher than the previous or pass. Winning bidder calls trump (Hearts automatic if bid was Solo in Hearts or Go Alone in Hearts) and, if not going alone, calls a card as partner; the holder of that card is the secret partner. Play: player to dealer's left leads. Players must follow suit if possible; if unable, must play a trump if able. No requirement to beat the card led. Winner of each trick leads the next. Solo team's trick points are combined; 61 or more wins the hand. Scoring: Points awarded for making bid. Penalties for...",
