    "history": "Introduced in Nevada casinos in 1995 by Masque Publishing. Based on the lack of 10s which favors the house. - 1995: Debut in Las Vegas. - 2000s: Becomes a standard offering globally. - Present: Known for having a comparable house edge to Blackjack if played optimally. Australian Pontoon is essentially Spanish 21 with different terminology ('Pontoon' for Blackjack, 'Stick' for Stand). Attracts players who enjoy the bonus payouts and the 'fun' rules like Late Surrender.",
