    "rules": "Objective: Beat the dealer's hand total without going over 21. A hand total of 21 is best; player 21 always wins, including against dealer blackjack. Gameplay: Players place a bet. Dealer gives two cards to each player and two to himself (one dealer card face-up). Players act in turn: hit (draw), stand (pass), double down, split pairs, or surrender. Player 21 always wins. Player blackjack beats dealer blackjack. Late surrender and double-after-split are allowed. Dealer then plays according to house rules (hit or stand on soft 17). Hands are compared; higher total without busting wins. Bonuses pay for 6-7-8, 7-7-7, and multi-card 21. Scoring: Beat dealer's total without busting. 21 is best. - Spanish deck: 48 cards (no 10s); face cards count 10. - Late surrender allowed. Double after split and re-split aces allowed. - Player may double on any number of cards. Hit and double after...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Do not use standard Blackjack strategy! The missing 10s change the math significantly. You hit more often on stiff hands (12-16) because the bust card (10) is gone. You double less often against dealer's 2-6 because dealer is less likely to bust. Intermediate: Surrender: Use the 'Double Rescue' option freely if your double goes bad (e.g., Doubling 11, getting a 2 for 13 against a dealer Ace? Surrender). Advanced: Bonus Hunting: Sometimes hitting a hard 14 (composed of 7-7) against a dealer 6 is correct to fish for the third 7. - Tip: Never split 10s (Face cards). - Tip: Always hit 12 vs 2-3.",
