    "description": "Four-player trick-taking game of the Schafkopf group (ace-ten family), played mainly in north-eastern Michigan, USA. Temporary partnerships each hand (two vs two or one vs three). Trumps are all queens, jacks, and diamonds; the diamond 7 (Spitzer) ranks...",
