    "history": "Trappola originated in Venice (Cardano, 1564) and spread to Central Europe, where it developed many variations. Stovkahra (Brčko) is a surviving form played in the Czech village of Šumice in Romania's Banát region. Researched by Tomáš Svoboda in 1997 and published in The Playing-Card; it retains Trappola point values and bonuses using a German 32-card pack after original Trappola cards ceased production in 1944. - 1900s: Common in Slovak villages. - 1997: Researched by Tomáš Svoboda; rules published in The Playing-Card (IPCS). Features melding similar to Marias (Marriage = 20/40). A staple game for partnerships.",
    "setup": "Players: 4 (Partners sit opposite). Deck: German suited 32-card pack (7 to Ace); eight cards each in 3-2-3 packets; bottom card shown for trump. Equipment: German suited 32-card pack (7 to Ace); eight cards each in 3-2-3 packets; bottom card shown for trump. Dealing: Deal 8 cards each (4-4 or 3-2-3). Last card turned for Trump.",
