    "history": "Swingo Poker was invented by Steve Albini in December 2007 and developed by the Alliance-X poker group in Chicago; it is named after a song by Naked Raygun. Sweet Chariot is a lowball variation of Swingo: same structure but the lowest hand wins at showdown. - 2007: Swingo invented by Steve Albini. - Thereafter: Sweet Chariot played as lowball variant of Swingo. Sweet Chariot inverts Swingo's showdown: lowest hand wins instead of highest, using the same shared-card and borrow-one-opponent-board-card structure. Developed in Chicago poker circles; reflects home-game variant culture of shared-card poker.",
    "setup": "Players: Two to eight players; best with five to eight. Deck: Standard 52-card pack without jokers. Equipment: Standard deck, poker chips. Stakes (blinds and pot limit) agreed before play. Dealing: Small blind by player to dealer's left, big blind by the next player (twice small). Dealer shuffles and deals five cards face down to each player. First betting round; then each player chooses two hole cards and three board cards; all expose board cards. Second betting round. Dealer deals one shared river card face up to the centre. Third betting round. Showdown: lowest hand wins.",
