    "overview": "Tablić (or Tablanette) is a fishing-style card game popular in the Balkans (Serbia, Croatia, Bosnia). Players capture face-up cards from the table by matching their value or summing to their value. Points are awarded for capturing specific high-value cards (face cards, 10s, Aces) and for having the most cards. The game is similar to Casino. Origin: Balkans / Eastern Europe Players: 2-4 Deck: Standard 52-card deck Difficulty: Intermediate Duration: 20-30 minutes",
    "history": "Derived from the Casino family of fishing games; widely played in the former Yugoslavia. - 20th century: Popular across former Yugoslavia; rules published in English (Phillips & Westall 1939). A classic pastime in Balkan countries, often played by children and adults.",
    "setup": "Players: Normally two players, or four in fixed partnerships with partners sitting opposite. A three-player game is also possible but less usual; in Serbia deal and play are counter-clockwise. Deck: Standard 52-card deck Equipment: Cards, score sheet Dealing: Dealer deals 6 cards to each player and 4 face up on the table. Only the first deal places cards on the table. Subsequent deals refill hands until the deck is exhausted.",
    "rules": "Objective: Score points by capturing cards. Scores: A, K, Q, J, 10 = 1 point. 10 of Diamonds (Double Ten) = 2 points. 2 of Clubs (Little Two) = 1 point. Most cards = 3 points. Tabla (clearing the table) = 1 point. Gameplay: Players play one card from hand. If it matches a card on table (by rank) or a sum of cards (e.g. 9 captures 9, or 5+4), the player captures them. If no capture, the card stays on table. The player who makes the last capture takes any remaining cards at the end. Scoring: Card values: K=14, Q=13, J=12. Ace=1 or 11. Numerals=Face value. Scoring Points: K, Q, J, A, 10s = 1 point each. 10♦ = 2 points. 2♣ = 1 point. Tabla = 1 point (clearing table during play). Most cards = 3 points. - Capture by equality or sum - K=14, Q=13, J=12, A=1/11 - Tabla bonus for clearing table - Last capture takes remainder Win condition: Score points by capturing cards. Scores: A, K, Q, J, 10...",
    "strategy": "Basic: Capture as many point cards as possible (10, J, Q, K, A, 2♣). Prioritize the 10♦ (2 points). Try to clear the table (Tabla) for bonus points. Intermediate: Do not leave cards on the table that sum to easily captured numbers (like 11-14) if opponents likely hold face cards. Save high cards to make large captures. Advanced: Track the 10♦ and 2♣. Calculate remaining points. In endgame, try to make the last capture to sweep the board. - Tip: Kings (14), Queens (13), Jacks (12) can capture sums. - Tip: Aces can be 1 or 11 - flexible. - Tip: Clearing the table is worth a point (Tabla) - except at the very end.",
