    "rules": "Objective: As declarer, be the first to empty your hand to win and collect stakes from each opponent; as an opponent, empty your hand first to make the declarer lose and pay each of you. Gameplay: 1. Deal: Each player takes 10 cards one at a time in counterclockwise order from the face-down deck. 2. Bidding round 1: In turn, each player may declare (become declarer; play starts immediately) or pass. 3. If all pass, bidding round 2: Each may call for a card (name rank and suit; holder gives it face-up, you give one face-down in exchange) or pass; last player to call is declarer. If all pass again, redeal. 4. Play: Declarer leads any legal combination. Each in turn may beat it (same type, higher rank) or pass. Three consecutive passes clear the table; the last player to have played leads any legal combination. 5. First player out of cards wins the hand: if declarer, they win; if an...",
