    "history": "Tapp Tarock arose in Austria, possibly in the late 18th century; mentioned in Viennese works by 1806. Oldest rules description dates to 1821. - Late 18th century: Game likely developed in Austria. - 1806: Tarocktappen mentioned in Viennese comic opera and letters. - 1821: First printed rules in Vienna. - 19th–20th century: Played in Germany and Austria; four-player variants such as Königrufen developed. Originally had Tapper, Dreier, Solo bids; Tapper (use all six talon cards) was soon dropped. Modern bidding has Dreier, Unterer, Oberer, Solo with optional announcements (win last trick with Trump I, or Valat). Was the preferred card game of Viennese coffee houses before the Anschluss; still played sporadically. Considered a good introduction to Tarock before Cego, Illustrated Tarock, or Königrufen.",
