    "variations": "- Taper (three players): Three-player form. 42-card pack (remove lowest three cards of each suit). No king called; declarer always plays alone against two in partnership. Twelve cards each, 6 to talon. Lowest bid unul de trei (take three from talon). Declarations 10, 11 or 12 taroace. No rege ultimo; no michi-michi (if all pass, cards thrown in and radler of three hands at double stakes). - Michi-michi: Played when all four players pass. Talon set aside; twelve tricks under usual rules but objective is to avoid winning tricks. No card points, declarations or bonuses. Each player pays one game point to the pool per trick won. Next four hands played at double stakes (radler)."
