    "setup": "Players: Four players; temporary partnerships (declarer plus holder of called king vs others, or declarer alone vs three). Deck: 54-card Taroki pack: 22 trumps (skiż, XXI down to I) and four eight-card suits (K, Q, C, J plus four pips). Equipment: 54-card Taroki pack, score sheet Dealing: Dealer deals 6 cards face down to table (talon), then remaining 48 in batches of 6 so each player receives 12 cards; anticlockwise. Player opposite dealer may refuse to cut; then dealer deals 6 to talon and four packets of 12, and each player in turn chooses a packet.",
    "rules": "Objective: Declarer's team wins by capturing more than half the card points (at least 35 of 70) in tricks plus their share of the talon. Opponents win if they have 35 or more. Game and bonuses (trul, last-trick-with-lowest-trump, kings, etc.) are scored and paid independently. Gameplay: Deal: 6 cards to talon, then 12 to each player in two rounds of 6; anticlockwise. Optional throw-in if dealt no taroks; optional declaration of four kings before bidding. Bidding: Forant (right of dealer) starts; each player once may bid 1–4 (talon cards to take) or pass; 4 only after a 3. Declarer calls a king by suit; its holder is partner (secret). Optional king ultimo, kontra. Talon exchange: declarer takes 0–3 cards per bid, discards same number; may not discard 5-point cards or taroks unless unavoidable. Announcements: trul, last-trick-with-lowest-trump, taroki count, etc., in anticlockwise order...",
