    "history": "Three Card Poker was invented in England in the mid 1990s by Derek Webb. It was originally called Casino Brag, inspired by 3-card Brag, and was adapted so players bet against the house rather than each other. The name Three Card Poker was adopted when the game was introduced to America; it is also known as Tri Poker. Derek Webb's Prime Table Games marketed it to casinos; in 1999 Shuffle Master (later SHFL Entertainment) acquired the rights. - 1994: Patent filed. - Late 90s: Adopted by US casinos. - Present: A standard game in casinos worldwide. Derived from Brag. A staple introduction to casino poker for beginners.",
