    "history": "Tong-its gained popularity in the 1990s in Luzon, the largest island of the Philippines. Its precise origin remains undocumented, but it is widely believed to have been introduced or influenced by US military presence in the 1940s and adapted from the American card game Tonk (1930s). The game was evolved and popularized among Ilocanos as Tong-its and spread to regions such as Pangasinan by the mid-1980s, where it is also known as Tung-it. Both the name and structure suggest a direct relationship to Tonk; Tong-its is effectively an extended version played with 12-card hands. - Late 20th century: Tong-Its appeared in the northern Philippines, extended version of Tonk with 12-card hands. Derived from Tonk and Mahjong mechanics. A favorite pastime in the Philippines.",
