    "rules": "Objective: Win all 52 cards by capturing the opponent's cards through comparison; the player who ends up with all the cards wins. Gameplay: Both flip top card. Higher wins both (placed at bottom). Tie = War: 1 face-down then 1 face-up each. Higher face-up wins all cards in the war. Multiple wars possible. Insufficient cards during war = lose. Scoring: Win all cards or opponent runs out. - Simultaneous flip - War on ties - 1 face-down then 1 face-up during war - No player decisions Win condition: Win all 52 cards.",
    "strategy": "Basic: No strategy — pure luck. Intermediate: None. Advanced: None.",
    "variations": "- Three face-down war: In a war, each player plays three cards face down then one face up (ten cards total). Whoever has the higher face-up card wins all ten. If a player has fewer than four cards, some play that the player with fewest cards uses all their cards and the other plays the same number. - War with two jokers: Two jokers are added to the pack and count as the highest cards, above aces. To avoid one player getting both, some separate the jokers before dividing the deck and bury one joker in each player's stack."
